                "reply_count": 17,
                "retweet_count": 7,
                "source": "Twitter for iPhone",
                "text": "Miami\u2019s future depends on smart, proactive policy. The Terrorism Risk Insurance Act (TRIA) isn\u2019t just an abstract program, it safeguards our schools, hospitals, and neighborhoods. I\u2019m glad the Committee is treating this issue with the urgency it deserves, and I strongly support reauthorizing this critical protection.\n\nFor me, this is especially important because the University of Miami, right in my district, relies on TRIA to secure affordable coverage for its hospitals, research facilities, and stadiums. Without it, both the University and the broader Miami community would be left vulnerable to devastating losses.",
                "text_lang": "en",
                "text_tagged_users": null,
                "text_tagged_users_ids": null,
